+# S004 Data Model — Provider retry quota
+
+This is a logical model. Map it to the project’s existing persistence conventions during implementation; no datastore or table names are evidenced in this workspace.
+
+## Workspace retry quota
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace that owns retry credit. | Identifies one authoritative quota balance. |
+| `available_retry_credits` | Credit currently available to reserve. | Integer, non-negative. Decrement only in the same transaction/conditional write that creates a reservation. Increment only while restoring a `reserved` reservation. |
+
+## Retry reservation
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `attempt_id` | Stable identifier for one reminder send attempt. | Unique idempotency key; carried into provider completion, error, timeout, and cancellation paths. |
+| `workspace_id` | Owning workspace. | Must match the quota balance mutated by this reservation. |
+| `state` | Reservation lifecycle. | One of `reserved`, `finalized`, `restored`. |
+| `created_at` | Reservation time. | Set on successful reserve. |
+| `terminal_at` | Time of the first terminal transition. | Set only when leaving `reserved`. |
+| `terminal_reason` | Recorded terminal outcome. | Required for `restored`; may record provider acceptance for `finalized`. |
+
+## Relationships and invariants
+
+- One workspace has one authoritative retry-quota balance and zero or more retry reservations.
+- One attempt has exactly one retry reservation. A second reserve for the same `attempt_id` returns the existing reservation rather than decrementing credit again.
+- `reserved` → `finalized` does not change the available balance again: the initial reservation already consumed the credit.
+- `reserved` → `restored` increments the available balance exactly once.
+- `finalized` and `restored` are terminal. No transition may leave a terminal state.
+- A reservation is created only if the same atomic operation proves `available_retry_credits > 0`; therefore concurrent attempts cannot make the balance negative.
+
+## Transition table
+
+| Operation | Required current state | New state | Balance effect | Duplicate outcome |
+|-----------|------------------------|-----------|----------------|-------------------|
+| Reserve | No reservation for `attempt_id`; balance > 0 | `reserved` | Decrement 1 | Return existing reservation; no mutation. |
+| Finalize | `reserved` | `finalized` | None | Return persisted terminal state; no mutation. |
+| Restore | `reserved` | `restored` | Increment 1 | Return persisted terminal state; no mutation. |
+
+## Migration and recovery
+
+- Add the reservation storage and its uniqueness constraint before routing sends through it.
+- Backfill is not specified because existing quota storage and historical attempts are absent from this workspace. Keep the change additive and decide any backfill against the real schema during implementation.
+- A durable `reserved` record remains the recovery anchor for timeout/cancellation handling; do not delete it before a terminal outcome is recorded.
